  "scope": "Pooled automatic threshold across frozen plane targets in the C++ core/Python API and managed executor. Shared ordinary Z-stack ImGui checkbox selects/locks all slices; preview and Apply use the same target membership and pooled level.",
  "behavior": "A reusable histogram solver preserves selected legacy method conventions. The pooled helper scans one plane/mask at a time, with no concatenated pixel buffer. It uses ROI members for estimation, validates entire acquired planes, skips source acquisition for empty masks, and applies the common threshold through existing masked output/publication/type policies. Endpoint exclusions still affect estimation only. Native target API supports captured C/Z/T positions; complete scientific threshold controls in the UI remain open.",
  "profile": "Finite-only scalar sources, plane execution, 2..65536 bins (0=>256), selected sample count <=INT32_MAX. Integer histograms use full type range; float histograms use global selected extrema. Legacy mean/constant shortcuts can finish after one scan; histogram construction uses two. Providers must remain immutable across reads. Empty selection/eligible histograms and invalid working caps refuse without edits.",
  "reference": {
    "scope": "Six-method thresholds use retained pinned uniform/endpoint Java histograms. The same 256 samples are split across four source planes, each contributing one quarter of that histogram. UInt8/UInt16/Float32/Float64 bin-center expectations are independently derived from the retained expected bin. Eighteen-method logical-concatenation compatibility is a separate check, not an independent upstream oracle.",
