  "checks": "Per OS: 3716 distinct selected checks, no failures/errors/skips. 96 exact pooled histogram/type/endpoint cases, 18 logical-concatenation method comparisons, scientific ROI/position writes, captured navigation/stale publication, preflight/cancellation/callback failure, empty targets and admission checks, 12 workflow serialization/replay cases and 24 new actual-input UI reports. Previous 3542 threshold/numeric/desktop/AVI/registry/jobs checks remain passing. 72 physical reports / 6816 frames per OS include old selector/endpoint regressions; 15 transport tests also pass. Nineteen further callback checks verify standalone 0/1..1/1 progress, reentry, completion cancellation and exact managed plane counts.",
  "resource_scope": "Managed reservations include histogram tables and conservative nested fallback workspace plus existing output/plane/mask budgets. Public scratch cap covers dense buffers, tables and rounded raster admission; frozen arguments, other ROI geometry scratch, opaque callbacks, provider caches, source/history/allocator/process memory remain external. Preview currently stages detached outputs for the selected stack, not only the visible slice. Full global allocation/latency/large-data certification is open.",
  "commercial_scope": "No new runtime dependencies, Java, Qt or non-commercial components. Reviewed commercial-use inventory passes on Windows/Linux; installed audit matches 70 source headers, 12 Python modules and 92 registered operations.",
  "source_review": [
    "Extracted the old histogram solver for shared plane/pool execution; preserved no-option constant/raw-mean shortcuts and endpoint-aware fallback behavior. Old numeric/reference checks pass.",
    "The GUI automatically selects and disables all-slices while pooling is enabled; preview uses that same scope.",
    "Core target mask merge/publication/type rules remain authoritative; no separate Python pixel implementation.",
